027Q1 contracts at 95.5 imply 4.50%, and the 2027Q4 contract at 96.0 implies 4.00%.\n  - The market therefore prices about 50bp of cuts by end-2027 (`cma_futures`).\n  - Governor Ashby's base case is one 25bp cut in 2027. She also said markets \"may be getting ahead of themselves.\"\n  - The gap is about 25bp of easing that is priced in but not guided.\n- **Sensitivity:**\n  - The factsheet says a 50bp lower policy path historically lifts the basket P/E by about 1.5 points. The weighted forward P/E is 19x.\n  - If the market moves to the CMA's path, that is roughly 0.75 points of P/E lost, so about 19x falls to about 18.25x. That is a drop of roughly 4%.\n- **Earnings:**\n  - Consensus expects 2027 EPS growth of 14%, driven by backlog conversion at Voltaris and Tarnwell. Estimates have risen 3% over the past quarter.\n  - A 14% earnings gain is much larger than a 4% multiple compression. Even with the de-rating, the basket's implied value still rises by roughly 9–10%.\n- **Risks:**\n  - The multiple is exposed to a hawkish CMA surprise. A \"no cuts\" outcome would be a roughly 1.5-point de-rating, about 8% if the sensitivity holds.\n  - The EPS estimates rest on backlog conversion at two names, which together are 25% of the fund (Voltaris 14%, Tarnwell 11%).\n  - The P/E sensitivity is a historical average and may not hold.\n- **Not checked:** I did not look at the option pricing. That is the separate question n3 is working on.","ttft_ms":4975,"type":"result","duration_ms":36189,"uuid":"3c045c92-cfba-4f54-b571-d1d0a1e83db8","ttft_stream_ms":3803,"time_to_request_ms":61,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":12,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":1,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":5,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_bui